      "id": "no-output-runs-no-blocker",
      "agent": "auto",
      "prompt": "Bug: review-only runs (swarm ask runs, review runs: every job declares outputs as an empty list) raise a blocker 'Run X is complete but not integrated: ...' even though there is nothing to integrate. In tools/autopilot.mjs, decide(run, ctx) treats any run with status complete and no integrated flag as needing integration, returns the action integrate, and the step that handles it (around the integrationBlocker check) writes a blocker with id integrate-checkout-RUN. Fix: a run with no integrable outputs must never raise that blocker, never get an integrate action, and never produce the integration needs-a-decision blocker. How: find where the run objects passed to decide are built (search tools/swarm.mjs, tools/autopilot.mjs and tools/monitor-view.mjs for where status, integrated, counts and pause are assembled for autopilot) and add a boolean field integrable that is true when at least one job of the run declares a non-empty outputs list (read it from the saved manifest or the job records; keep the field name integrable); in decide return null (no action) for a complete, not integrated run whose integrable is explicitly false; a run record without the field (older state) keeps today's behavior. Also close blockers that were already raised for such runs: when autopilot sees an open blocker whose id starts with integrate-checkout- or integrate- for a run whose integrable is false, it writes a resolution event for it (use the same event kind the other resolutions use, find it in tools/autopilot.mjs and tools/inbox.mjs) so it disappears from Needs you. Do not change behavior for runs that have outputs. Tests in a new file tests/autopilot-no-outputs.test.mjs (node:test, strict assert, fakes like tests/autopilot.test.mjs): a complete review-only run (integrable false) gets no action and no blocker even when the checkout is not on a swarm branch; a complete run with outputs (integrable true) still gets the integrate action and still gets the checkout blocker when the checkout is wrong; a run without the integrable field behaves as before; an open integrate-checkout blocker for a review-only run is closed; a mix of both runs in one pass; plus one test that builds the run view from a saved state of a swarm ask style run (jobs with empty outputs) and asserts integrable is false, and from a state with outputs asserts true. Write only tools/autopilot.mjs, tests/autopilot-no-outputs.test.mjs and, only if the run view is built there, tools/swarm.mjs and tools/monitor-view.mjs.",
